        "route": "Core",
        "hours": 1.4166666666666667,
        "scope": "The CPU executes instructions, RAM holds working state, and storage retains data across restarts. Virtual memory gives each process an address space rather than direct ownership of all RAM. Performance symptoms and security evidence depend on which layer is involved; high disk use is not automatically malware.\n\nDeeper-study checklist: CPU instruction cycle, RAM, persistent storage. Use the section references to investigate these terms and connect them to the practice evidence.",
