      {
        "id": "CS02-L02",
        "title": "Processes, threads and privilege",
        "stage": "CS02",
        "domain": "CS02",
        "domainName": "Computers, operating systems and data",
        "route": "Core",
        "hours": 1.4166666666666667,
        "scope": "A process owns resources and an execution context; threads share parts of that process. User and kernel modes separate ordinary programs from privileged operating-system work. A child process can inherit access or handles. Least privilege limits damage when a process behaves incorrectly.\n\nDeeper-study checklist: Process isolation, threads, privilege rings. Use the section references to investigate these terms and connect them to the practice evidence.",
        "practice": "Draw a process tree for a browser or editor. Identify its user and explain which operations require elevated rights; use read-only inspection tools.",
