        "route": "Core",
        "hours": 1.4166666666666667,
        "scope": "Bits represent values; hexadecimal is a convenient notation for bytes. Text encodings map characters to bytes, while Base64 represents bytes as printable text. Encoding is reversible without a secret and does not provide confidentiality. Unicode normalization and ambiguous characters can affect identifiers and validation.\n\nDeeper-study checklist: Bits, bytes, endianness, Unicode, Base64. Use the section references to investigate these terms and connect them to the practice evidence.",
