        "domainName": "Network services and packet analysis",
        "route": "Core",
        "hours": 1.4166666666666667,
        "scope": "DNS translates names into records through caches, resolvers and authoritative servers. TTL affects caching, not whether an answer is safe. DNSSEC authenticates signed DNS data where validation is deployed; it does not encrypt every query or certify a site's content.\n\nDeeper-study checklist: Recursive and authoritative DNS, caching, DNSSEC. Use the section references to investigate these terms and connect them to the practice evidence.",
        "practice": "Follow resolution for a domain you control or a training name. Record record types, TTLs, resolver choice and where cached answers change the observation.",
