            "title": "DNS resolution and trust",
            "kind": "Study",
            "minutes": 25,
            "instructions": "DNS translates names into records through caches, resolvers and authoritative servers. TTL affects caching, not whether an answer is safe. DNSSEC authenticates signed DNS data where validation is deployed; it does not encrypt every query or certify a site's content.\n\nDeeper-study checklist: Recursive and authoritative DNS, caching, DNSSEC. Use the section references to investigate these terms and connect them to the practice evidence.\n\nThink about this: What does DNSSEC not guarantee?",
