            "title": "Windows objects and access control",
            "kind": "Study",
            "minutes": 25,
            "instructions": "Windows access depends on identities, security tokens, object permissions and policy. NTFS permissions and network-share permissions interact but are not the same control. An administrative group membership does not mean every process is running with a fully elevated token.\n\nDeeper-study checklist: SIDs, access tokens, DACLs, UAC. Use the section references to investigate these terms and connect them to the practice evidence.\n\nThink about this: Why review both share and NTFS permissions?",
