        "hours": 2.1666666666666665,
        "scope": "An origin combines scheme, host and port. Cookies have scope and security attributes; web storage has a different access and lifetime model. Browser isolation, cross-origin policies and token storage must fit the application's design. Storing a secret in client-accessible storage expands the consequence of client-code compromise.\n\nDeeper-study checklist: Same-origin policy, cookies, local storage. Use the section references to investigate these terms and connect them to the practice evidence.",
