        "hours": 2.1666666666666665,
        "scope": "Security strength depends on the distribution of possible secrets and the attacker's information, not merely the number of visible characters. Human-selected passwords are not uniformly random. Distinguish uncertainty, probability and worst-case assumptions before making claims about resistance to guessing.\n\nDeeper-study checklist: Probability, entropy, combinatorics, threat assumptions. Use the section references to investigate these terms and connect them to the practice evidence.",
