        "hours": 2.1666666666666665,
        "scope": "A cryptographic hash maps data to a fixed-length digest under security assumptions. A checksum mainly detects accidental changes. An unkeyed digest does not prove who supplied a file; an attacker may replace both data and digest. A MAC uses a shared secret to authenticate a message.\n\nDeeper-study checklist: SHA families, collision resistance, HMAC. Use the section references to investigate these terms and connect them to the practice evidence.",
