            "id": "learn",
            "title": "Enterprise wireless and rogue infrastructure",
            "kind": "Study",
            "minutes": 40,
            "instructions": "Enterprise wireless combines device or user credentials, authentication servers and certificate validation. A convincing network name does not prove the access point or identity service is legitimate. Client validation, managed profiles and monitoring reduce exposure to unauthorized infrastructure.\n\nDeeper-study checklist: 802.1X, EAP, RADIUS, certificate validation. Use the section references to investigate these terms and connect them to the practice evidence.\n\nThink about this: Why is the SSID not a trustworthy identity?",
