      {
        "id": "CS42-L02",
        "title": "Prompt injection and untrusted content",
        "stage": "CS42",
        "domain": "CS42",
        "domainName": "AI, machine-learning and agent security",
        "route": "Core",
        "hours": 2.8333333333333335,
        "scope": "An assistant may encounter instructions embedded in retrieved pages, documents or tool responses. Those sources are data, not authority to change the user's goal or access policy. Strong boundaries require application controls over tools, identities and sensitive actions; a warning in a prompt alone is insufficient.\n\nDeeper-study checklist: Indirect prompt injection, instruction hierarchy, untrusted documents. Use the section references to investigate these terms and connect them to the practice evidence.",
