        "route": "Core",
        "hours": 3.75,
        "scope": "A blockchain combines a data structure, consensus and economic or trust assumptions. It does not make every external fact true or remove application governance. Private keys can control irreversible actions; custody, authorization and recovery need explicit design. Study with local test networks and no real funds.\n\nDeeper-study checklist: Consensus, wallets, custody, transaction finality. Use the section references to investigate these terms and connect them to the practice evidence.",
